# Operating Hints
- Read `AGENTS.md` first; it is the canonical project manual. This file covers execution discipline only.
- The user picks Teal or C# per session. Wait for the choice.
- Never run `tpr`. Use `scripts/render-check.sh` (`-h`). It fails on text overlap. `--skip-overlap` is only for intentional overprints.
- `scale-type.sh` and `ship-check.sh` already run render-check. Do not re-run render-check after either. The final gate is one `ship-check.sh --doc <slug>` run.
- Read the smallest slice. Use `rg`, `sed` ranges, and `repo-intel` before whole files. Whole-file reads are only for a style fingerprint: `:root`, `font-size` declarations, section/class skeleton, and one render function.
- For style fidelity, start from the closest sibling's palette, type scale, spacing, and structure. Expand beyond that fingerprint only when a needed pattern is missing.
- For visual checks, use one low-res montage or crop of the changed region per iteration. Never read `preview.html`, `output/**/*.html`, or 300dpi PNGs. Use render-check numbers and `read_image` crops only when visual verification is mandatory.
- Reflect after a task when the same text/math/command sequence recurs. Recommend a script only when it is recurring and deterministic. Do not add scripts for one-off work.
